 "summary": "Retired `DrillDownConfig.report`'s `{ name }` arm on all three faces, with no alias window, per triage ruling 5962814975. TS face: `report?: SpecReportInput`. Zod (tolerant and strict, since strict derives from the mirror): the report member is `stripImportedDefaults(SpecReportSchema)` plus two named refusals. `objectName` is declared through `aliasKeyRefusal` (names objectui#11506), which closes the reviewer note 5963125397: the tolerant face used to read the pre-9.0 form as `{ name }` and report it valid. A `superRefine(..., { when: () => true })` names a bare `{ name }` (`params.code` DRILL_REPORT_REFERENCE_RETIRED, names objectui#11517 and the dataset-bound remedy). For JSON values the accept set equals the spec's ReportSchema. The drawer is comment-only and draws the same thing; the docs drill section and two pending changesets are updated; there is a new `@object-ui/types` minor changeset. Draft PR #11527 is open, assigned os-tesla. The worktree and node_modules were removed after the PR opened.",
 "tests": "All at head ecf5fd38 (source bytes identical from 4b461bfa; ecf5fd38 adds only .changeset files). types type-check (3 legs) exit 0. The first run was red with TS2322 x2 from my own pin's control, fixed before commit; tsconfig.test.json --listFiles lists all 6 changed types tests. plugin-dashboard type-check exit 0 after `pnpm --filter @object-ui/types build`. console type-check exit 0 after building its 35-package closure; --listFiles lists the new console pin. `pnpm exec vitest run --maxWorkers=2 packages/types/`: 345 files, 9180 passed, VERDICT command-exit 0. A 27-file run (5 console, 2 cli, 1 plugin-grid, 10 plugin-dashboard drill/drawer, 9 scripts/__tests__ that read a changed file by path): 906 passed, VERDICT command-exit 0. eslint --no-inline-config --format json over the 11 changed ts/tsx files: 11 files, 0 errors, 34 warnings, all on untouched lines. Narrowing proof: population read from eslint.config.js ignores; count from the json output; invariance because there is no parserOptions.project or projectService and no eslint-rules file reads the fs. Reverse verification ran from committed head through objectstack scripts/ablation-replace.mjs; each leg landed on disk (anchor 1->0, blob changed) and restore was proven (blob == HEAD, `git diff HEAD` empty). A1, refinement dropped: predicted 6 red, observed 6 failed / 73 passed. A2, `objectName` undeclared: predicted 7, observed 7 failed / 72 passed. A3, `| { name: string }` back on the TS face: predicted 5x TS2578 + 1x TS2344; observed those plus TS2322 LedgerMismatch in zod-mirror-parity, so the direction was more diagnostics than predicted. A4, BASE union arm restored: predicted 16, observed 17 failed / 58 passed. The unpredicted one is the boundary row: the restored arm also read an incomplete inline report as `{ name }`. In A4 the console pin's refusal leg went red and its draw leg stayed green. TS face before/after per value was measured with a scratch tsc program that restates BASE's member type: `{ name }` and `{ name, columns: [] }` went accepted -> TS2741; the pre-9.0 form and `{ name: 42 }` are refused both times; the incomplete matrix and the dataset report are accepted both times.",
