  "name_only": "Same on both zod faces (mirror path `report`; object-pivot `properties.drillDown.report`; chart `drillDown.report`): code `custom`, params.code `DRILL_REPORT_REFERENCE_RETIRED`, message: \"`drillDown.report` as a named reference, `{ name }`, is RETIRED (objectui#11517): no renderer resolves a report name, so such a drill listed the records and drew no report. Write the report inline, dataset-bound: `@objectstack/spec`'s `ReportSchema`, `{ name, label, dataset, values, … }` (`values` are measure names; `rows`, and `columns` on a matrix, are dimension names), or a `joined` report whose `blocks` bind a dataset.\" The spec's own `invalid_union` at `report.label` ('Invalid input') is reported first.",
  "objectName_form": "Same on both zod faces, at `report.objectName`: code `invalid_type`, message: \"Unrecognized key(s) on this drill report: `objectName`. Did you mean `objectName` → `dataset`? The pre-9.0 object-bound drill report, `objectName` plus column objects, is RETIRED (objectui#11506): it had no producer, and the drawer drew no report for it. Write the dataset-bound form: `dataset`, `values` (measure names), and `rows`, and `columns` on a matrix, as dimension names.\" The spec's own issues (`report.label` invalid_union, `report.columns.0` invalid_type) are reported beside it. Before this change the tolerant face accepted this value, and the strict face refused it as `unrecognized_keys` in the spec's words."
 },
